<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eurocommunism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1970s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eurocommunism was a trend among West European communist parties in the 1970s and 1980s, led by the Italian party under Enrico Berlinguer and the Spanish party under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> Carrillo. Eurocommunists claimed independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and accepted parliamentary democracy and civil liberties. The Soviet suppression of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-spring">Prague Spring</a> in 1968 did much to inspire the movement.</p></div>
